  "face.panel.corners": "The notch's edge (0.553,1.811)-(0.365,1.601) drawn as straight chamfers: the smoothed curve through four close points wobbled 1.1 mm (the shared smooth-edge check).",
  "face.shapes.dots": "Each dot a circle of r 0.045 (rect with full corner radius) instead of a 12-point polygon, which the smooth-edge check reads as a 2 mm wobble.",
  "doors.w": "Passenger doors 1.40 m (the 320/3 diagram drew 1.703; published clear opening 1.20 m). The model's door is the hole in the bodyside, front jamb to the rear jamb's outer edge, which on the 318 measured 0.29 m wider than its published 1.010 m opening (p258); p304 reads 1.32 m centred 7.19 m (rear jamb u 1775 to the leaves' front edge u 1822, through a 1D projective fit on the bottom row of the window frames, residuals 1.2 px, heavily foreshortened: +-0.15 m). Leaf windows scaled with the leaf: 0.17..0.54 m from the centre line.",
  "face.number": "On the near side: image right of the face on p404 (near side seen) and p304 (far side seen, so the face's right is the near side); the close render drew it on the far side with m > 0.",
  "liveries.SR.branding": "The ScotRail logo (logos/SR.svg, one colour), size as measured on the 318 (classes/318 trace: 0.90 m high, 2.29 m wide, the same vinyl on the same body): the 320's lettering on p304 reads 105 px against the window frame's 302 px for 1.06 m above it, 0.37 m (318: 0.41 m). Cab car: on p304 (far side) between doors 1 and 2, its extremes u 1645..1710 at 9.63..11.37 m through a 1D projective fit on the window frames' bottom row (residual 1.2 px, foreshortened: +-0.3 m), centre x 10.5; lettering centre 141 px under the window frame (2.044 m), y 1.55. Saltire towards the rear on the far side, as the default turned-round far-side placement draws it. Second car: mid-car on p304 (the MSO, thumb x 455-475), centred in the gap between its doors at the same height; not measured further."
 },
